description:
0383d5e (437) corrected src/ingest/stages/auth.ts:6-11 to say an enabled-auth 401 DOES persist a transmission row. The identical falsehood 437 describes survives one file away, in the file that implements the exception.

src/ingest/route.ts:65-68, inside preBodyStages():

    // Stage 2 - Auth (opt-in, 1.3, M6/ct4.2). When the session has opted in,
    //   a missing/incorrect credential short-circuits 401 like 404/405 with no
    //   transmission row; the zero-friction default (auth disabled) is a no-op.

That is false for exactly the reason 437 gives, and route.ts now contradicts itself three ways over: its own module header at route.ts:11-13 ('An enabled-auth 401 (stage 2) DOES persist a row'), its handler comment at route.ts:214-221, and the code at route.ts:224-228 (haltedAt === 'auth' -> persistTransmission). auth.ts:6-11 now points AT route.ts for the special case, so a reader following that pointer lands on the stale claim.

Comment-only; no behaviour change. Same fix as 437, applied to the site the sweep missed. Consider also softening the preBodyStages doc comment at route.ts:51 ('a halt here writes no row'), which is the general framing the auth exception breaks.
